{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"When exclusions leave chat with no candidate, the request fails as expected but its error omits the exclusion reason."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A queued chat can send its private conversation to a model whose origin became prohibited while it waited for capacity."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A panel review can fail after selecting an excluded verifier even though an eligible verifier is available."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A resumed evaluation can run a trial before failing on a prohibited model in its saved escalation chain."},{"id":"C6","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The private-output error repeats an identical exclusion reason for each affected model."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"The reproduced short source line is a cosmetic Markdown wrapping issue with no rendered effect."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The reproduced behavior accepts the roster configuration at startup but routes to an eligible alternative, so the claimed review failure is not established."}]}